{
  "about": "Serial 123 point 7 (amendment 1): an address found in prose ends where its own grammar cannot continue. After the id (or a world alone), `@` and a moment and `?lens=` and a lens continue it; any other query key or a fragment is not part of an address found in prose, and the address ends before its `?`, `&` or `#`. readOwLinkAt(text, index) / read_ow_link_at(text, index) reads the address starting exactly at index and answers its reading and `end`, the index just past it; each case's `address` is the slice text[index:end] it must cover, and `reading` is what the whole-string parser answers for that slice. null when the text at index is not an address. `index` defaults to 0. Kept byte for byte in both packages. A lens ends where its id ends (36 characters); a moment is its whole run of an optional minus and digits and is taken only when that run reads as one step.",
